ORCHESTRATOR-DERIVED READINGS FROM THE PASTED TEXT
--------------------------------------------------
Labelled as derived, NOT as operator observations. The operator said only "It looked ok".

(1) MAIN-phase firmware frame count corroborates Gate 3 independently.
    The MAIN phase shows exactly 6 `DATA:` lines between each pair of `OK: Request
    data` boundaries, across 4 blocks = 24 frames, at a uniform 164-byte step
    (164, 328, 492, 656, 820, 984 | 1188 … 2008 | 2212 … 3032 | 3236 … 4056).
    That equals plan 145-07's `intra_block_frames=24` exactly, from a SEPARATE run
    on a separate invocation. Because these are `DATA:` decode lines rather than
    tqdm redraws, this is a third oracle for D-10 Claim A/B, independent of both the
    extractor and 145-07's own `-v` decode.

(2) The 164-byte cadence is consistent with the 1000 ms emission interval.
    At 4688 us pulse plus 145-07's derived ~1436 us per-byte overhead, per-byte cost
    is ~6124 us; 164 x 6124 us = ~1004 ms, i.e. one frame per ~1000 ms cadence.
    1024/164 = 6.24, giving the observed 6 frames per 1024-byte block.

(3) NEW FINDING — the write progress bar never reaches 100%.
    The final MAIN bar frame reads `0x0fd8/0x1000` = 4056/4096 = 99.02%, yet the
    write succeeded (`Write to W27C512 successful (30.94s)`). The bar stalls at the
    LAST firmware progress frame because no final frame is emitted at completion.
    Verified reproducible across every write captured this phase:
      - Gate 3, 145-07 recorded run  : 0x0fd8/0x1000   (4056/4096,   99.02%)
      - Gate 3, this eyes-on re-run  : 0x0fd8/0x1000   (4056/4096,   99.02%)
      - Gate 2 cycle 1               : 0xfeb0/0x10000  (65200/65536, 99.49%)
      - Gate 2 cycle 2               : 0xfeb3/0x10000  (65203/65536, 99.50%)
      - Gate 2 cycle 3               : 0xfeb0/0x10000  (65200/65536, 99.49%)
    The INIT blank-check bar DOES reach 100% (`0x10000/0x10000` above), so this is
    specific to the MAIN write bar, not to progress rendering generally.
    Scope note: cosmetic/UX only — every one of these writes verified byte-exact, so
    no correctness claim is affected. Out of scope to fix here (D-16 forbids any plan
    editing firestarter/ or firestarter_app/); recorded as a finding to carry forward.

(4) The D-10 contradiction, stated rather than reconciled.
    Operator impression: "It looked ok". Artifact: the bar terminates at 99% on this
    run and on all four other writes this phase. These are not reconciled here. The
    honest reading is that a bar stopping one frame short of full is not something a
    casual observer would flag, which is precisely why D-10 requires both halves and
    forbids collapsing one into the other.
